Firmware from ROCKNIX extra-firmware
Source: https://github.com/ROCKNIX/extra-firmware, commit e1eb71af80427aa1fec1659d2967f7ba8bef83b5,
SM8550/ directory

Files in this package taken from it (under /usr/lib/firmware):
  qcom/sm8550/ayn/cdsp.mbn, cdsp_dtb.mbn, qcom/sm8550/ayn/<device>/* (ADSP firmware and
  amplifier tuning), qcom/sm8550/<card>-tplg.bin (audio topology), qcom/vpu/vpu30_p4.mbn,
  ath12k/WCN7850/hw2.0/board-2.bin and regdb.bin

These are proprietary firmware images, not Kettle Linux's or ROCKNIX's own work: they come from
the device's vendor (AYN) and its chip vendor (Qualcomm), as ROCKNIX collected them for its
images. The ROCKNIX/extra-firmware repository states no licence for them, and the files carry
no licence text of their own.

Status: redistribution permission from the rights holders has NOT been recorded for Kettle
Linux. They are shipped pending that permission; this file grants no rights of any kind.

The other firmware in this package comes with its own licence files in this directory:
linux-firmware-qcom/ and linux-firmware-atheros/ (Arch's linux-firmware packages) and
ath12k-WCN7850-Notice.txt (upstream linux-firmware).
